<hr>
<p>We've reached the end of the array. Should we go back to the start of th=
e array to check if starting from station 6 allows us to complete the circu=
it? Or is reaching the end from station 6 enough to finish the circuit? Let=
's look into this.</p>
<p><strong>Proving we have enough gas to complete the circuit after reachin=
g the end of the array</strong><br>
<!-- -->We can determine this via a proof by contradiction. If the gas we h=
ave by the end of the array is not enough, that means no solution exists: n=
o station at which we could start in order to complete the circuit. This im=
plies that no matter where we start, we will hit a deficit (i.e., a point w=
here our tank falls below 0) before completing the circuit.</p>
<p>Consider a segment of the circuit where we run into a deficit:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
